coe(a){switch(a.toUpperCase()){case"CA":return"These Terms are governed by the laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein, without regard to conflict of law provisions. Disputes shall be resolved by binding arbitration under the Arbitration Act, 1991 (Ontario), conducted in English in the Province of Ontario, or remotely by mutual agreement.\n\nYou waive any right to participate in a class action proceeding, except where prohibited by applicable law."
case"GB":return"These Terms are governed by the laws of England and Wales. Any dispute shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of England and Wales, without prejudice to our right to seek injunctive relief in any jurisdiction."
case"AU":return"These Terms are governed by the laws of New South Wales, Australia. Any dispute shall be subject to the non-exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of New South Wales."
case"DE":case"FR":case"NL":case"ES":case"IT":return"These Terms are governed by the laws of the Ontario, Canada, without prejudice to mandatory consumer protection provisions of your country of residence under European Union law. You may also bring proceedings before the courts of your habitual residence."
default:return"These Terms are governed by the laws of the Ontario, Canada, without regard to its conflict of law provisions. Any dispute arising out of or relating to these Terms or the App shall be resolved by binding arbitration or another lawful dispute process permitted by applicable law, conducted in English. Either party may seek emergency injunctive relief in a court of competent jurisdiction in Ontario, Canada.\n\nYou waive any right to participate in a class action lawsuit or class-wide arbitration against the Company. This waiver is enforceable to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law."}},
cog(a){switch(a.toUpperCase()){case"CA":return"Under PIPEDA and Ontario's PHIPA, you have the right to:\n\u2022 ACCESS: Request access to your personal health information\n\u2022 CORRECTION: Request correction of inaccurate information\n\u2022 WITHDRAWAL: Withdraw consent to collection or use at any time\n\u2022 COMPLAINT: File a complaint with the Office of the Privacy Commissioner of Canada (priv.gc.ca) or the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Ontario (ipc.on.ca)\n\nTo exercise your rights: thecontessaapp@gmail.com"
case"GB":return"Under UK GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, port, and object to processing of your personal data. You may lodge a complaint with the Information Commissioner's Office (ico.org.uk). Contact: thecontessaapp@gmail.com"
case"DE":case"FR":case"NL":case"ES":case"IT":return"Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), you have the right to access, rectify, erase, restrict, port, and object to processing of your personal data. You have the right to lodge a complaint with your national data protection authority. Contact: thecontessaapp@gmail.com"
case"AU":return"Under the Privacy Act 1988, you have the right to access and correct your personal information. You may lodge a complaint with the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (oaic.gov.au). Contact: thecontessaapp@gmail.com"
default:return"Depending on your jurisdiction, you may have the right to:\n\u2022 ACCESS: Request a copy of your personal data\n\u2022 CORRECTION: Correct inaccurate data\n\u2022 DELETION: Request deletion of your data\n\u2022 PORTABILITY: Receive your data in a machine-readable format\n\u2022 WITHDRAW CONSENT: At any time, for data processed on the basis of consent\n\nCALIFORNIA RESIDENTS: Under CCPA, you have additional rights including the right to know, delete, and opt out of sale of personal information. We do not sell personal information.\n\nTO EXERCISE YOUR RIGHTS: Email thecontessaapp@gmail.com with \u201cPrivacy Request\u201d in the subject line."}},
