B.cq0=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Headache and swelling can be useful context to track together, but one mild headache plus one swelling log is not, by itself, a preeclampsia alert. It becomes more important if the headache is severe, persistent, worsening, or paired with vision changes, high blood pressure, right upper abdominal pain, or sudden/extreme face or hand swelling.",2,"Escalate urgently for severe or persistent headache, visual symptoms, elevated blood pressure, right upper abdominal pain, or sudden/extreme face or hand swelling.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, NHS"])
B.cqa=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Headache with visual change is a high-priority pregnancy warning-sign combination associated with hypertensive complications.",1,"Same-day clinical review is appropriate, especially after 20 weeks.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her"])
B.cq8=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Swelling with visual symptoms is more concerning than swelling alone and can indicate a preeclampsia-related pattern rather than routine fluid retention.",1,"Escalate promptly if symptoms are new, worsening, or involve the face and hands.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her"])
B.cqj=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Headache on the same day as elevated blood pressure is a high-priority pregnancy warning-sign combination. It can be relevant when reviewing possible hypertensive complications, especially after 20 weeks.",1,"Same-day provider review is appropriate for headache with elevated blood pressure, especially if severe, persistent, or paired with visual symptoms, swelling, or right upper abdominal pain.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her"])
B.cpP=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Swelling on the same day as elevated blood pressure can be useful context for a preeclampsia-focused review, especially when swelling is new, sudden, or involves the face or hands.",1,"Review blood pressure readings, swelling location/severity, headache, vision changes, and right upper abdominal pain with a provider.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her"])
B.cq2=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Elevated blood glucose and elevated blood pressure appearing on the same tracked days is clinically meaningful pregnancy context. Each can warrant provider review on its own, and together they should not be averaged away as routine tracking noise.",1,"Review recent blood pressure and glucose readings together, including timing, symptoms, medications, gestational week, and any provider thresholds already given.","ACOG, ADA, CDC Hear Her"])
B.cpN=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Reduced baby movement on the same day as elevated blood pressure deserves prompt attention. Reduced fetal movement should be reviewed based on provider guidance, and blood pressure adds important clinical context.",1,"Contact the care team promptly for reduced fetal movement, and include the blood pressure reading when calling.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, NHS"])
B.cpO=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Reduced baby movement on the same day as elevated blood glucose is meaningful context for provider review. The movement change is the priority signal, with glucose adding clinical background.",1,"Contact the care team promptly for reduced fetal movement, and include the glucose reading and timing when calling.","ACOG, ADA, NHS"])
B.cpX=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Sleep disruption and headache can reinforce each other. This is useful context when reviewing hydration, blood pressure, stress, pain, or medication factors.",2,"Review if headaches are severe, persistent, worsening, paired with high blood pressure or vision changes, or if sleep loss is impairing daily function.","ACOG, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cq6=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Very little sleep on the same day as marked irritability can be clinically meaningful perinatal mental-health context, especially if it is new, escalating, paired with racing thoughts, agitation, panic, intrusive thoughts, or feeling unlike yourself.",1,"Review sleep duration, mood intensity, racing thoughts, panic/agitation, intrusive thoughts, medication/supplements, support at home, and safety concerns.","ACOG, WHO, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpM=new A.eo([B.fL,"Recurring","Sleep disruption and irritability can reinforce each other and may be worth reviewing when the overlap repeats or affects functioning.",2,"Discuss if sleep loss and irritability are recurring, worsening, impairing functioning, or paired with anxiety, panic, racing thoughts, or intrusive thoughts.","ACOG, WHO, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqi=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Elevated heart rate on the same tracked day as elevated blood pressure is clinically meaningful context for provider review, especially with headache, vision changes, chest pain, shortness of breath, dizziness, fever, or feeling unwell.",1,"Review blood pressure, pulse value, timing, repeat readings, symptoms, hydration, medications/supplements, fever, pain, anxiety, and provider-specific thresholds.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqk=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Chest pain with elevated heart rate needs urgent clinical review because cardiopulmonary causes must be considered.",1,u._,"ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpS=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Shortness of breath with elevated heart rate can be clinically important and should not be treated as routine pregnancy discomfort without context.",1,"Prompt clinical review is appropriate, especially if symptoms are new, worsening, resting, or paired with chest pain, fainting, or leg swelling.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqf=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Dizziness with elevated heart rate can be useful context when reviewing hydration, blood pressure, blood sugar, anemia, infection, medication effects, or anxiety.",1,"Review pulse, blood pressure, hydration, glucose, fever, bleeding, medications/supplements, and whether dizziness includes fainting or chest symptoms.","ACOG, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cq7=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Fever with elevated heart rate can indicate systemic illness or infection and deserves prompt review in pregnancy or postpartum recovery.",1,"Review temperature, pulse, symptoms, hydration, urinary symptoms, uterine or breast pain, and clinical escalation thresholds.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpZ=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Fever with back pain can indicate infection, including pyelonephritis, and should not be treated as routine discomfort.",1,"Prompt provider review is recommended, especially with urinary symptoms or chills.","ACOG, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqh=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Fever with cramping may reflect infection or a concerning uterine pattern depending on gestation and context.",1,"Prompt review is appropriate if symptoms are persistent, worsening, or accompanied by discharge or bleeding.","ACOG, NHS"])
B.cpT=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Chest pain with shortness of breath requires urgent assessment because serious cardiopulmonary causes must be ruled out.",1,u._,"ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpU=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Itching with jaundice is a clinically meaningful combination because it raises concern for hepatobiliary disease such as cholestatic patterns.",1,"Liver-focused provider review is recommended.","NHS, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqb=new A.eo([B.fL,"Recurring","Anxiety and insomnia are meaningfully related because they can reinforce each other and worsen daily functioning during pregnancy or postpartum recovery.",2,"Discuss if this is impairing daytime function or persisting.","WHO, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cq5=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Irregular sleep can add useful context when reviewing glucose readings, appetite, stress, and daily routines. This does not explain a high reading by itself, but the overlap is worth tracking.",1,"Review glucose timing, meals, sleep disruption, stress, medication/supplements, and provider-specific glucose thresholds.","ADA, ACOG, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cqc=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Irregular sleep can add useful context when reviewing blood pressure, stress, pain, and headaches. Elevated blood pressure should still be interpreted using provider guidance and pregnancy warning-sign thresholds.",1,"Review blood pressure readings alongside sleep disruption, headache, vision symptoms, swelling, pain, stress, and medications.","ACOG, CDC Hear Her, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpR=new A.eo([B.fL,"Recurring","Nausea and vomiting commonly travel together, but repeated overlap matters most when hydration, nutrition, or weight maintenance are affected.",2,"Escalate if fluids cannot be kept down or dehydration signs appear.","ACOG"])
B.cpV=new A.eo([B.bY,"Alert","Breast pain with fever is a clinically meaningful postpartum combination that can indicate mastitis or another breast infection.",1,"Prompt evaluation is appropriate, especially with redness, warmth, or flu-like symptoms.","ACOG, NHS, Mayo Clinic"])
B.cpQ=new A.eo([B.f3,"Watch","Breast soreness with night sweats is only clinically useful when accompanied by fever, chills, redness, or feeling unwell. On its own, this pair is nonspecific.",2,"Escalate only if systemic infection features are present.","ACOG, NHS, Mayo Clinic"])
