B.cfG={Nausea:0,Vomiting:1,Fatigue:2,"Back Pain":3,Heartburn:4,Insomnia:5,Anxiety:6,Depression:7,Dizziness:8,Itching:9,Constipation:10,"Leg Cramps":11,"Round Ligament Pain":12,"Braxton Hicks":13,"Mood Swings":14,"Food Aversions":15,"Frequent Urination":16}
B.cNt=new A.fm(7,12,22,4,7,14,7,"Daily nausea every day this week may indicate hyperemesis \u2014 seek provider support.","Persistent nausea pattern. Small frequent meals and ginger can help.","Nausea is very common in pregnancy, especially first trimester.")
B.cNs=new A.fm(5,8,15,3,5,10,4,"Frequent vomiting risks dehydration \u2014 consider IV fluids if unable to keep water down.","Recurring vomiting. Stay hydrated with small sips throughout the day.","Occasional vomiting is normal. Try eating dry crackers before getting up.")
B.cN3=new A.fm(7,13,25,5,9,18,7,"Extreme persistent fatigue \u2014 check iron levels and thyroid function.","Significant fatigue pattern. Prioritise rest and iron-rich foods.","Fatigue is normal in pregnancy. Rest when you can.")
B.cNb=new A.fm(5,9,18,3,5,10,5,"Persistent back pain \u2014 rule out kidney infection or preterm labour.","Regular back pain. Pregnancy pillow and gentle stretching can help.","Back pain is common due to postural changes. Avoid heavy lifting.")
B.cN7=new A.fm(6,11,20,4,7,14,7,"Daily heartburn significantly impacting quality of life \u2014 medication options available.","Frequent heartburn. Avoid spicy foods and eat smaller meals.","Heartburn is very common in second/third trimester due to hormones.")
B.cN2=new A.fm(6,11,20,4,7,14,7,"Chronic insomnia affecting health \u2014 discuss safe sleep options with provider.","Regular sleep disruption. Try a pregnancy pillow and sleep hygiene routine.","Sleep changes are common. Short naps and relaxation techniques can help.")
B.cN5=new A.fm(5,8,15,3,5,10,4,"Persistent anxiety in pregnancy needs support \u2014 mental health matters as much as physical.","Recurring anxiety noted. Mindfulness, support groups, and therapy can help.","Some anxiety is normal in pregnancy. Talk to someone you trust.")
B.cNa=new A.fm(3,5,8,2,3,5,3,"Persistent low mood needs professional support. Perinatal depression is treatable.","Regular low mood pattern. Please speak to your midwife or provider.","Low mood can occur during pregnancy. Reach out to someone you trust.")
B.cNc=new A.fm(4,7,12,2,4,8,3,"Frequent dizziness \u2014 check blood pressure and blood sugar levels.","Recurring dizziness. Rise slowly and stay hydrated.","Occasional dizziness is common. Avoid standing quickly.")
B.cNl=new A.fm(5,8,14,3,5,10,4,"Persistent itching \u2014 especially hands/feet \u2014 needs liver function testing (cholestasis risk).","Regular itching noted. Mention to provider at next appointment.","Skin stretching causes itching. Moisturise regularly.")
B.cNm=new A.fm(5,9,16,3,5,10,5,"Severe constipation \u2014 safe stool softeners available, discuss with provider.","Regular constipation. Increase water, fibre, and gentle movement.","Constipation is very common in pregnancy due to progesterone.")
B.cNj=new A.fm(5,9,16,3,5,10,5,"Frequent leg cramps \u2014 check magnesium levels.","Regular leg cramps. Magnesium supplement and calf stretches can help.","Leg cramps are common, especially at night. Stretch before bed.")
B.cNr=new A.fm(6,11,20,4,7,14,7,"Persistent sharp side pain \u2014 rule out appendicitis or ovarian issues.","Regular ligament pain. Move slowly when changing position.","Round ligament pain is normal and caused by uterine growth.")
B.cN6=new A.fm(7,13,25,5,9,18,7,"Regular tightening \u2014 if rhythmic or painful, rule out preterm labour.","Frequent Braxton Hicks. Stay hydrated and rest.","Braxton Hicks are practice contractions \u2014 very normal after 20 weeks.")
B.cNp=new A.fm(6,11,20,4,7,14,7,"Extreme mood instability \u2014 consider screening for perinatal mental health.","Regular mood changes noted. Hormonal fluctuations are the cause.","Mood swings are very common. Be kind to yourself.")
B.cNo=new A.fm(7,13,25,4,7,14,7,"Strong aversions affecting nutrition \u2014 discuss dietary alternatives with provider.","Persistent food aversions. Focus on foods you can tolerate.","Food aversions are very common, especially in first trimester.")
B.cNq=new A.fm(7,13,25,5,9,18,7,"If accompanied by burning or pain, rule out UTI.","Regular urinary frequency is normal in pregnancy.","Frequent urination is very common due to uterine pressure on bladder.")
B.cdw=new A.an(B.cfG,[B.cNt,B.cNs,B.cN3,B.cNb,B.cN7,B.cN2,B.cN5,B.cNa,B.cNc,B.cNl,B.cNm,B.cNj,B.cNr,B.cN6,B.cNp,B.cNo,B.cNq],t.Mb)
