B.cKb=new A.o2("Tongue symptoms can relate to irritation, oral thrush, or feeding friction.","Look for white patches that do not wipe away, bleeding, refusal to feed, or worsening discomfort. If the tongue looks coated, sore, or feeding becomes painful or difficult, contact your pediatrician. Keep noting feeding changes and whether the symptom improves or spreads.",null)
B.cKc=new A.o2("Foot symptoms are often minor irritation, pressure marks, or positional changes, but should be watched closely in babies.","Check for swelling, color change, tight sleepers, hair tourniquet, or signs of pain when touched. If the foot looks blue, swollen, cold, or your baby seems very uncomfortable, seek urgent medical care. Otherwise keep tracking what you notice and whether it resolves quickly.",null)
